# Short-sentence emphasis

**A page of at most 4 words (`SHORT_SENTENCE_MAX_WORDS`) highlights exactly one word.** Two glowing words out of four reads as shouting, not emphasis.

- Words are counted with `countSentenceWords`: punctuation-only tokens (`—`, `…`) do not count.
- One word means one token, or one whole bound phrase / Vietnamese two-syllable compound (`im lặng`, `học sinh`). The compound rules still hold: never split a compound to meet the cap.
- Enforcement lives in `limitShortSentenceEmphasis` (`features/kinetic-text/lib/text-language/short-sentence-emphasis.ts`). Both `getEmphasizedWordIndexes` (feed) and `getPreviewEmphasizedWordIndexes` (preview) pass their final result through it, after `repairSplitCompoundEmphasis`, on **every** return path — data annotations, poetic phrases and scoring alike.
- Any new emphasis selector must end the same way. Do not raise a per-language run limit for short pages; the cap overrides it.
- Pages with 5+ words are unchanged.

Bad (4 words): `Mưa rơi rất nhẹ` with `Mưa` and `nhẹ` both highlighted; `là học sinh giỏi` with `học sinh giỏi` (3 tokens) glowing.

Good: `Mưa rơi rất nhẹ` → only `nhẹ`; `là học sinh giỏi` → `học sinh` (one compound); `Pause before replay` → one word only.

Verify with `scripts/check-emphasis-short-sentence.ts`.
